{"text": " You wake up in 1847 in Vienna. It's a cold morning on the maternity ward of the general hospital. Did you know that in the doctor's clinic here in April, about 18 and every 100 mothers died after giving birth? 18 and 100. Here's your patient, a new mother, a young doctor, Ignos Semovice notices that for years, mothers with the midwives have died far less often. He asks every doctor to wash their hands and chlorinated line before touching a patient. Reportedly, he picks it because it takes away the smell of the dead. He doesn't know about germs yet. Then he counts April 18 and 100, June about two, July about one, August about two. How long do you live? In Britain, a newborn could expect about 38 years. So what is medicine now, pattern? Count the deaths, then look for the cause. Most doctors reject his idea. He can show that it works. He can't show why that needs germs and a drug that goes after them. And the first patient to get one is a police officer in Oxford.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.8, "text": " You wake up in 1847 in Vienna.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 2443, 14060, 294, 31024, 13, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1390003895196389, "compression_ratio": 1.5859649122807018, "no_speech_prob": 0.005394762381911278, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.12, "probability": 0.7879047989845276}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.28, "probability": 0.9878249168395996}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.28, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.9995527863502502}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.6, "probability": 0.990814745426178}, {"word": " 1847", "start": 0.6, "end": 1.78, "probability": 0.9923281371593475}, {"word": " in", "start": 1.78, "end": 2.46, "probability": 0.8582533597946167}, {"word": " Vienna.", "start": 2.46, "end": 2.8, "probability": 0.9784356355667114}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 3.6, "end": 5.4, "text": " It's a cold morning on the maternity ward", "tokens": [50542